2Ki 23:1 , Josiah causes the book to be read in a solemn assembly;
2Ki 23:3 , He renews the covenant of the Lord;
2Ki 23:4 , He destroys idolatry;
2Ki 23:15 , He burns dead men's bones upon the altar of Beth-el, as was fore-prophesied;
2Ki 23:21 , He keeps a most solemn passover;
2Ki 23:24 , He puts away witches and all abomination;
2Ki 23:26 , God's final wrath against Judah;
2Ki 23:29 , Josiah, provoking Pharaoh-nechoh, is slain at Megiddo;
2Ki 23:31 , Jehoahaz, succeeding him, is imprisoned by Pharaoh-nechoh, who makes Jehoiakim king;
2Ki 23:36 , Jehoiakim's wicked reign.
